            <div xml:id="d546">

                <pb facs="0969" n="873" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg873"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.342/–: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kreeck</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-10-20T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 20,
                                1926—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>13. Legation’s cable No. 12, October 5, 5 p.m. Department is pleased to learn
                    that the Foreign Minister is favorably disposed towards negotiating a treaty. A
                    draft of the treaty and instructions are being prepared and will go forward
                    shortly by pouch.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
